<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Bartłomiej Wójtowicz</title><link>https://qbart.dev/</link><description>Recent content on Bartłomiej Wójtowicz</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-gb</language><copyright>Bartłomiej Wójtowicz</copyright><lastBuildDate>Sat, 07 Nov 2026 15:07:49 +0100</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://qbart.dev/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Release: assetc 0.2.0, the asset compiler rebuilt in Rust</title><link>https://qbart.dev/posts/2026/release-assetc-rust/</link><pubDate>Sat, 07 Nov 2026 15:07:49 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://qbart.dev/posts/2026/release-assetc-rust/</guid><description>assetc is rebuilt from scratch in Rust: a CLI and Bevy/egui editor that compiles textures, glTF models, materials, shaders, fonts and game data into runtime formats, plus a dependency-free SDK crate for the game side.</description></item><item><title>Release: meshopt-pure 1.3.0, meshoptimizer in pure Rust</title><link>https://qbart.dev/posts/2026/release-meshopt-pure/</link><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 20:17:08 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://qbart.dev/posts/2026/release-meshopt-pure/</guid><description>An unofficial pure Rust port of meshoptimizer v1.3 with bit-identical output, SIMD decoders and no C dependencies, plus gltfpack and clusterlod in the same repository.</description></item><item><title>matma 0.2 and 0.3: splines, animation curves and monotone ramps</title><link>https://qbart.dev/posts/2026/matma-0-2-0-3-curves/</link><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 19:45:19 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://qbart.dev/posts/2026/matma-0-2-0-3-curves/</guid><description>Two follow-up releases of matma: 0.2.0 brings the curves module (Catmull-Rom splines, arc length, AnimationCurve), 0.3.0 adds MonotoneCurve, a Fritsch-Carlson cubic that never overshoots.</description></item><item><title>Release: ktx-rs 4.4.2, KTX-Software ported to Rust</title><link>https://qbart.dev/posts/2026/release-ktx-rs/</link><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 20:15:01 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://qbart.dev/posts/2026/release-ktx-rs/</guid><description>An unofficial Rust port of Khronos KTX-Software: libktx, the ktx CLI and the Basis Universal and ASTC encoders, byte identical to upstream and passing the full CLI conformance suite.</description></item><item><title>Release: matma 0.1.0, game math for Vulkan in Rust</title><link>https://qbart.dev/posts/2026/release-matma/</link><pubDate>Sun, 25 Oct 2026 21:38:32 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://qbart.dev/posts/2026/release-matma/</guid><description>SIMD-first math for games and Vulkan with Slang/HLSL naming, std140/std430 derives and GPU packing helpers. A Rust port of my C++23 library vkm, with no third-party dependencies.</description></item><item><title>assetc gets LOD controls</title><link>https://qbart.dev/posts/2026/assetc-gets-lod-controls/</link><pubDate>Sat, 19 Sep 2026 22:30:00 +0200</pubDate><guid>https://qbart.dev/posts/2026/assetc-gets-lod-controls/</guid><description>meshopt-based LOD generation is now tunable per-asset via assetc.yml, with retry/fallback for stalled simplification and a matching LOD selector in the inspector.</description></item><item><title>How to Build Learning Experience Platforms like 360Learning</title><link>https://qbart.dev/posts/2024/how-to-build-learning-experience-platforms-like-360learning/</link><pubDate>Mon, 15 Jul 2024 13:00:00 +0200</pubDate><guid>https://qbart.dev/posts/2024/how-to-build-learning-experience-platforms-like-360learning/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://selleo.com/blog/how-to-build-learning-experience-platforms-like-360learning?utm_source=qbart.dev&amp;amp;utm_campaign=qbart.dev"&gt;Article here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>What Are the Challenges of Implementing Gamification in Education Platforms?</title><link>https://qbart.dev/posts/2024/what-are-the-challenges-of-implementing-gamificati